{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2198-12-04 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee. You were brought in because of nausea and vomiting. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2198-12-04 09:25:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes… I woke up this morning feeling fine, but then my blood sugar was in the 200s, and I started vomiting. It’s just like my last flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2198-12-04 09:26:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, and you’ve had this before with your gastroparesis. Are you able to keep anything down at all?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2198-12-04 09:26:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not even water. I threw up once this morning and it’s been nonstop since."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2198-12-04 09:27:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Your blood pressure is quite high—210 over 100—and your heart rate is fast, 140. That’s common during these episodes, but we’ll need to manage it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2198-12-04 09:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It always goes up when I’m sick. But I stopped my blood pressure meds a few days ago… I thought I didn’t need them anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2198-12-04 09:28:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be part of why it’s so high. We’ll restart those, but for now, we’re giving you fluids and medications through your port to help with the nausea and vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2198-12-04 09:29:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. My stomach just won’t settle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2198-12-04 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve given you Zofran, Compazine, and Ativan for nausea. Your labs show your blood sugar was high—323—and your bicarbonate is a bit low, which means mild acidosis. But no severe ketoacidosis this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2198-12-04 10:16:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So not DKA again? I was so sick last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2198-12-04 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, not full DKA. You have trace ketones, but your anion gap is closing. We’re continuing your long-acting insulin and using a sliding scale for corrections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2198-12-04 10:18:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What about my liver tests? I saw something about elevated enzymes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2198-12-04 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your ALT and AST are elevated—69 and 82—higher than usual for you. But they weren’t extremely high, and we don’t think it’s from Tylenol or infection. We’ll check them again at your follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2198-12-04 10:20:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t taken any Tylenol. Could it be from the Botox injection I had six months ago?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2198-12-04 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly, but we don’t have proof. The GI team thinks your symptoms are more related to your gastroparesis flaring up again. They recommend restarting Reglan and continuing pantoprazole."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2198-12-04 10:22:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember Reglan helps. But will I need another Botox injection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2198-12-04 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The GI team suggested considering it during your outpatient colonoscopy, especially since you have iron deficiency anemia. You’ll discuss that with your gastroenterologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2198-12-04 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. And my gastric pacer—should the settings be adjusted?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2198-12-04 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you should follow up with Dr. ___ to evaluate if the neurostimulator settings need changing. That could help reduce these flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2198-12-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing better—no vomiting since last night. You’re on IV fluids and your blood sugars are stabilizing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2198-12-05 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I feel a bit better. Can I try drinking something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2198-12-05 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with small sips of water. If you keep that down, we’ll advance to clear liquids and then soft foods."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2198-12-05 08:33:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. And my blood pressure? It was so high yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2198-12-05 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave IV metoprolol yesterday, and now we’re restarting your home meds—lisinopril and metoprolol twice daily. Your heart rate is down to 90 today, which is much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2198-12-05 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to take them regularly from now on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2198-12-05 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning show your bicarbonate is up to 24, so the acidosis has resolved. Liver enzymes are trending down slightly too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2198-12-05 14:21:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. So I’m improving on all fronts?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2198-12-05 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ve kept down apple juice and crackers. We’ll move you to a soft diet and plan for discharge tomorrow if this continues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2198-12-05 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. What meds will I go home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2198-12-05 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue glargine insulin at night and the humalog sliding scale. Also, Reglan with meals, pantoprazole daily, and your blood pressure meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2198-12-05 14:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the Zofran and Compazine for if I get nauseous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2198-12-05 14:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, Zofran ODT as needed every eight hours, and Compazine suppositories up to twice a day. But avoid driving with those—they can make you drowsy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2198-12-06 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’ve tolerated a full soft meal and no vomiting. We’re clearing you for discharge today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2198-12-06 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful. What should I do at home to prevent this from happening again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2198-12-06 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Eat small, frequent meals and stay upright for at least 30 minutes after eating. Keep up with your Reglan and pantoprazole. And don’t skip your blood pressure meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2198-12-06 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I need to schedule the colonoscopy and see my GI doctor?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2198-12-06 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Also follow up with your primary care doctor to review your liver tests and medication plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2198-12-06 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my husband has my emergency contact info, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2198-12-06 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we have his number. Call us if you start vomiting again, can’t keep insulin down, or your blood sugar goes very high or low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2198-12-06 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you so much for helping me through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2198-12-06 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did well. We’ll get your discharge papers ready, and you should be home within a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2198-12-06 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave—still feeling okay? No nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2198-12-06 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I feel much better. I even had toast and tea this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2198-12-06 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Remember to take your meds as prescribed and follow up with your doctors."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2198-12-06 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2198-12-06 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2198-12-04 09:24:00",
    "admission_end": "2198-12-06 16:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of Type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis, and GERD was admitted for nausea and vomiting, consistent with a gastroparesis flare. She had recently stopped her blood pressure medications, leading to hypertension and tachycardia. She was treated with bowel rest, IV fluids, antiemetics, and insulin therapy. Her symptoms improved, she advanced to a soft diet, and her lab abnormalities, including mild acidosis and elevated liver enzymes, resolved or trended toward normal. She was restarted on home medications including lisinopril, metoprolol, Reglan, and pantoprazole, and discharged home in stable condition with follow-up plans for colonoscopy, possible Botox injection, and gastric pacer evaluation.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Esophagitis, unspecified",
      "Nonspecific elevation of levels of transaminase or lactic acid dehydrogenase [LDH]",
      "Tachycardia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
